        "original_id": "be0ae338-c1cc-5bc0-af50-7aacbbaba92d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leading chiefs of the Seminoles, Micanopy\n- Organizations: Seminole tribe, United States Government\n- Places: Indian Territory, Indian country\n- Events: Second Seminole War\n- Concepts: Native American relocation, aboriginal title\n\nFacts:\n- The Seminole tribe organized in the mid-18th century.\n- Leading chiefs of the Seminoles were leaders from the tribe’s organization in the mid-18th century until the 1830s.\n- Indian Territory, the Indian Territories, and Indian country were general terms for an evolving land area set aside by the United States Government.\n- The United States Government set aside Indian Territory for the relocation of Native Americans who held aboriginal title to their land.\n- Micanopy and many Seminole were removed to Indian Territory in the 1830s after the Second Seminole War.",
